<BotanicalConsortium>
  <Families>
    <Family>
      <familyId>FAM01</familyId>
      <familyName>Asteraceae</familyName>
      <description>The Asteraceae family, commonly known as the aster, daisy, or composite family, is a very large and widespread group of flowering plants with over 32,000 species.</description>
    </Family>
    <Family>
      <familyId>FAM02</familyId>
      <familyName>Rosaceae</familyName>
      <description>Rosaceae is a medium-sized family of flowering plants, including about 4,828 species in 91 genera, characterized by showy flowers with five petals and numerous stamens.</description>
    </Family>
    <Family>
      <familyId>FAM03</familyId>
      <familyName>Liliaceae</familyName>
      <description>Liliaceae consists of monocotyledonous, perennial, herbaceous, often bulbous geophytes with large flowers and are traditionally used extensively in decorative gardening and floral arrangements worldwide.</description>
    </Family>
    <Family>
      <familyId>FAM04</familyId>
      <familyName>Orchidaceae</familyName>
      <description>Orchidaceae is a diverse and widespread family of flowering plants, with blooms that are often colorful and fragrant, representing one of the two largest families of flowering plants.</description>
    </Family>
    <Family>
      <familyId>FAM05</familyId>
      <familyName>Iridaceae</familyName>
      <description>Iridaceae is a family of plants in the order Asparagales, taking its name from the Iris genus, containing roughly 66 genera and totaling over 2,244 species globally.</description>
    </Family>
    <Family>
      <familyId>FAM06</familyId>
      <familyName>Lamiaceae</familyName>
      <description>Lamiaceae or Labiatae is a family of flowering plants commonly known as the mint or deadnettle or sage family, containing many widely used culinary and medicinal herbs.</description>
    </Family>
    <Family>
      <familyId>FAM07</familyId>
      <familyName>Ranunculaceae</familyName>
      <description>Ranunculaceae, the buttercup or crowfoot family, is a family of over 2,000 known species of flowering plants distributed worldwide, especially in temperate and cold regions of the Northern Hemisphere.</description>
    </Family>
    <Family>
      <familyId>FAM08</familyId>
      <familyName>Papaveraceae</familyName>
      <description>Papaveraceae is an economically important family of about 44 genera and 770 species of flowering plants in the order Ranunculales, often known colloquially as the poppy family.</description>
    </Family>
    <Family>
      <familyId>FAM09</familyId>
      <familyName>Boraginaceae</familyName>
      <description>Boraginaceae is the borage or forget-me-not family, including a variety of shrubs, trees, and herbs totaling about 2,000 species in 146 genera found across the globe.</description>
    </Family>
    <Family>
      <familyId>FAM10</familyId>
      <familyName>Fabaceae</familyName>
      <description>Fabaceae or Leguminosae, commonly known as the legume, pea, or bean family, is a large and economically important family of flowering plants with distinct fruit structures called legumes.</description>
    </Family>
  </Families>

